    "Nothing has been deleted. Here's what the preview shows.\n\n**If you approve, deleting your local Google data would:**\n1. Remove the locally stored Google tokens.\n2. Cancel any active Google import or sync jobs.\n3. Permanently delete the local Google records and the raw responses kept on disk.\n\n**What that covers, based on the local database:**\n- **Google (API):** 3 daily step records, from 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-03.\n- **Google Takeout:** 1 daily step record, for 2026-10-01. The Takeout file is a separate provider. Deleting Google data only applies to `google_takeout` if you also request `include_takeout_data`, which I haven't included in this preview. Tell me if you want that too.\n\n**What this does not do:**\n- It does not revoke the app's access on Google's side. Your Google authorization stays active unless you ask for that separately.\n- It does not affect your Fitbit data.\n\n**Confirmation:** The preview token expires in 5 minutes. If you want me to go ahead, reply \"yes, delete my local Google data.\" If you also want Takeout data removed or Google authorization revoked, say so and I'll generate a new preview with those options."
